## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- Q16–Q20 should not become markdown headings. Korean source is plain "Q16." and English is the same body line, not `##`. checkHeadings compares heading levels to the Korean source. The bold "**16.**" form is what keeps the outline count.
- U+200B blank lines and the four `**​**` lines in 005 cannot be deleted. They are in the Korean source. checkBlocks fails if the ZWSP count or the block count moves. The spoken columns were repaired by closing each block as a sentence instead.
- "(no és l’article 10)" cannot be deleted. The suggested label drops the digit 10, and the checker then reports `missing from translation (1): 10`. The Korean label still says article 10 of the business-tax act; the URL is flno=3 of the withholding-rate standard. Article 3 and the statute name stay; the digit stays with them.
- The suggested join of "si es parla de massatge," with the next paragraph would merge two blocks. Each block was closed on its own.
- Reformatting "TWD 1.57M" would break the pinned bio token. The Catalan gloss "(1,57 milions de dòlars taiwanesos)" is already next to it.
